  "description": "Look at a Fuji Team. It looks\n\na lot like our expensive, limited-production Team Issue. Please do not think\n\nof it as the Team Issue’s little brother. The Mercury Cycling Team’s\n\nTeam Issue bicycles have precisely the same frame geometry as the Team bikes\n\nyou see at your Fuji dealer. Study the specs. Granted the Easton aluminum\n\nframe tubes are somewhat different and the seat stays are different, but the\n\nbikes are far more alike than their prices. Ride a Team and a Team Issue.\n\nYou may recognize that similarity. We hope you do: that’ll mean our production\n\nracer is nearly as stompin’ competent as the all-out, low-volume model\n\nwe build for Mercury.\n\nWhen you ride a Team Fuji, or study its specs, you will conclude that it is\n\namong the world’s elite racing bicycles. You will have concluded correctly.",
